	(text "external connection:\n(1) SMA with RG-58/U for 500V rating\n(2) pin header, covered with pin socket when\nnot in use (trim or cover leads of socket)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 30.988 123.698 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "3e6dae20-d3ab-4e9d-b578-e2de0ce770c6")
	)
	(text "0.185 W in resistor\n5.92 K temperature rise\n±1.48e-4 proportional change\n\n430 V on resistor\n-4.3e-4 proportional change\n\ntolerance on static gain: ±2e-3\nG = -35.64 (min.)\nG = -35.71 (avg.)\nG = -35.79 (max.)\n\ninput = -12.00 V\noutput = 427.7 V (min.)\noutput = 428.5 V (avg.)\noutput = 429.5 V (max.)\n\nThere is a slight offset of approximately\n-4.5 V, which varies slightly based on\nenvironment variables. The map from input\nto output is still extremely linear, with\nGoogle Sheets registering R^2 = 1 exactly\nfor a plot with 7 data points.\n\nSolution to the offset problem: slice the\nSENSEN connections at the interface between\nboards. Reconnect them to GND on the main board.\nNow the inputs of the PA95 are subjected to\neven higher voltage differentials, possibly up\nto the DAC's programmed voltage limits. But I\nchose to not add protection diodes or transistors.\n\nOffset is now +56 mV (cold), +76 mV (warmed up)\nwhen the DAC is using -12 V to 12 V range."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 30.734 31.242 0)
